+# hedgedoc-k8s
+
+A Kubernetes charm for HedgeDoc, written with the `ops` library. The charm
+source is in `src/` (`charm.py` for the Juju side, `hedgedoc.py` for the
+workload-facing `CMD_*` mapping, free of `ops`), unit tests (ops.testing /
+Scenario) in `tests/unit/`, integration tests (jubilant) in
+`tests/integration/`, and docs in `docs/`. Charm libraries fetched with
+`charmcraft fetch-lib` live under `lib/` and are listed under `charm-libs:` in
+`charmcraft.yaml`.
+
+## Commands
+
+- Unit tests: `tox -e unit` (or `uv run pytest tests/unit`)
+- Lint: `tox -e lint` (ruff check, ruff format --check, codespell)
+- Static checks: `tox -e static`
+- Charm linter: `uvx charmlint .`
+
+## Conventions
+
+- Keep the reconciler pattern: events funnel into `_reconcile`, and unit
+  status is set only in `_on_collect_status`.
+- Keep workload-facing logic in `src/hedgedoc.py`, free of `ops` imports.
+- Tests go through `ops.testing.State`, the Pebble plan and relation
+  databags; do not reach into private attributes of the charm.
+- `docs/reference/configuration.md` must match the option descriptions in
+  `charmcraft.yaml` (a unit test checks this).
